{"chapter": "topologies", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "022I", "placeholders": {"ACCENT_0001": "\\'e"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-contained-in}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:1832aafb7c6f0c607b61ea3a2e5702efa63a4e2054d73bb8583e9338697e6ee0", "source_text": "Any set of big Zariski sites is contained in a common big Zariski site.\nThe same is true, mutatis mutandis, for big fppf and big <ACCENT_0001>tale sites.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:c7a8f1519d4f9180c8aa2f4ccfa3f6a1798e38c1edf9dfb02b04c94fd090968b", "unit_id": "tag:022J:statement"}
{"chapter": "topologies", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "022I", "placeholders": {"REF_0001": "\\ref{sets-lemma-construct-category}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{sets-lemma-coverings-site}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:6f27f3559f25e84099954cd0cbfe538ed902381ef4cda50c0133f66184f5d543", "source_text": "This is true because the union of a set of sets is a set, and the\nconstructions in Sets, Lemmas <REF_0001> and\n<REF_0002>\nallow one to start with any initially given set of schemes\nand coverings.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:d7aaf359d0051280358cb7a5fb36d4dd078ade22ec5e3f72ccc5ac4beb7a2e6d", "unit_id": "tag:022J:proof"}
